  "description": "YEGYIV crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C115 H114 Dy4 F3 N18 Ni3 O27 S1 5+,5(C1 F3 O3 S1 1-),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.376-3.662 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.74-106.61°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [NiII3DyIII4(μ3-OH)6(L1)6(CF3SO3)](CF3SO3)5·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
